## Context

Experiment 1 establishes the parametric ceiling: best row-level F1 achievable from
model memory alone, no documents, no search. The current census sweep used
`prompt_extract.txt` (a one-sentence CSV request). We are replacing it with `base.txt`
(the structured table specification with column definitions), which is a more defensible
"competent analyst" baseline and avoids the strawman critique.

The pilot (25 runs, 10 models, `p1_base` prompt version) is too small to report.
This ticket upgrades to the journal-tier model set (9 models × 5 repeats = 45 runs)
and locks temperature at 0 to separate prompt-driven variance from sampling noise.

See Annex A in `slides/manuscript/main.md` for the full technical specification.

